# [TSVWG](../wg/tsvwg.html)

## Summary

The Transport and Services Working Group (TSVWG) met at IETF 121. The session covered working group document status updates, liaison updates, SCTP security key management alternatives, L4S operational and architectural updates (including Structured Rate Management and cellular performance), transport port registration guidance updates, ILNP checksum compatibility, WebRTC data channel acceleration via SCTP, UDP fragmentation socket guidance, and QUIC transport parameter implementation analysis. 

Working Group Last Call (WGLC) for [draft-ietf-tsvwg-fq-pie](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tsvwg-fq-pie/) concludes today. [draft-ietf-tsvwg-sctp-dtls-chunk](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tsvwg-sctp-dtls-chunk/) is prepared for WGLC. Key decisions include scheduling a design team meeting to resolve SCTP key management transition proposals prior to a formal list consensus call, and pursuing Independent Submission Stream publication for the ILNP checksum draft.

