### UDP Fragmentation
* Presentation: [UDP Fragmentation](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tsvwg-udp-fragmentation-01)
* Marten Seemann presented `draft-seemann-tsvwg-udp-fragmentation`, which documents operating system socket options and APIs for controlling UDP IP Don't Fragment (DF) flags, modeled after the ECN socket guidance in RFC 9715 / RFC 9656.
* **Poll 4**: *I have familiarized myself with the draft* — yes: 12, no: 27, no_opinion: 2 (total: 80)
* Michael Tuexen supported adoption and offered FreeBSD implementation code.

### QUIC Transport Parameters
* Presentation: [QUIC Transport Parameters and protocol designer thoughts](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-tsvwg-quic-transport-parameters-and-protocol-designer-thoughts-00)
* Lucas Pardue presented an analysis of open-source QUIC implementations regarding their handling of duplicate transport parameters and protocol greasing.
* The survey revealed six distinct implementation behaviors responding to the RFC 9000 `SHOULD` requirement for duplicate transport parameters, though all converged on detecting duplicates at the parameter ID layer.

